# IR Switch PCB

An infrared-controlled switch that detects IR signals and generates a stable output using a TSOP IR receiver and a 555 timer.

## Overview
This PCB allows remote switching using an IR transmitter. The received signal is conditioned using a 555 timer to produce a reliable output signal and visual feedback.

## Key Features
- TSOP17xx infrared receiver
- NE555 timer for signal conditioning
- LED output indicator
- Operates on 5 V DC
- Screw terminal connections

## Design Highlights
- Clean separation of sensor and timing circuitry
- RC network for stable triggering
- Visual LED feedback for signal detection

## Files Included
- IR Switch.kicad_sch – Schematic
